WEBVTT

00:00:00.450 --> 00:00:01.417
Hi, I'm Nacelle!

00:00:01.417 --> 00:00:05.287
A fan project runs Need for Speed Most Wanted in Chrome, online.

00:00:05.287 --> 00:00:08.833
The game sits behind a login, so here is the outside.

00:00:10.183 --> 00:00:14.343
The idea: it draws with WebGPU and pulls files from a download

00:00:14.343 --> 00:00:19.196
network, but its game logic is being rebuilt, one original behaviour at a time.

00:00:20.717 --> 00:00:24.395
Logged out, you get one page, a logo and two screenshots.

00:00:24.395 --> 00:00:25.733
No scripts, no WebAssembly.

00:00:26.153 --> 00:00:28.806
Its one check: does this browser have WebGPU?

00:00:29.353 --> 00:00:31.470
The game client loads only after login.

00:00:31.470 --> 00:00:32.680
I made no account.

00:00:33.100 --> 00:00:36.501
Files come from a storage bucket on a fast download network.

00:00:36.501 --> 00:00:38.046
Careers live on their server.

00:00:39.692 --> 00:00:42.062
Four ways to put an old Windows game in a tab.

00:00:42.558 --> 00:00:46.287
Recompile the studio's own source, as the GTA Five port did.

00:00:46.707 --> 00:00:49.233
Rebuild source from the binary, then compile it.

00:00:49.653 --> 00:00:52.440
Run the original program, translating as it goes.

00:00:52.440 --> 00:00:54.182
Slow, and hard to change.

00:00:54.602 --> 00:00:56.825
Or write a new engine around the game's data.

00:00:58.317 --> 00:01:01.820
If the original code ran, police would already follow the road map,

00:01:01.820 --> 00:01:04.740
and speeding would already start at a hundred and thirty.

00:01:05.160 --> 00:01:07.749
Instead the fixes say: now like the original game.

00:01:07.749 --> 00:01:09.475
And pieces of Carbon move in.

00:01:09.475 --> 00:01:11.489
That is code the team can edit.

00:01:12.967 --> 00:01:16.456
New features land daily, like a cockpit view with hands on the wheel.

00:01:16.876 --> 00:01:19.689
And a rear-view mirror, off on phones and in lite mode.

00:01:21.008 --> 00:01:25.475
The public decompilation of this game matches under fourteen percent of the PC code.

00:01:25.475 --> 00:01:27.389
Nothing links it to this site.

00:01:28.808 --> 00:01:32.706
Remember: fixes that restore the original are evidence of rewritten code,

00:01:32.706 --> 00:01:34.124
not the shipped program.

00:01:37.108 --> 00:01:41.887
WebGPU on screen, files from a bucket, the original rebuilt piece by piece.

00:01:42.307 --> 00:01:44.364
Every source is in the full article.

00:01:44.364 --> 00:01:44.952
I'm Nacelle.

00:01:44.952 --> 00:01:45.246
Bye!
